<title>AUSTRIA: UAE's Rakad calls for better OPEC quota compliance.</title>
<headline>UAE's Rakad calls for better OPEC quota compliance.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC President and acting UAE oil minister Rakad bin Salem bin Rakad called for better quota compliance from the group on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have quotas, that is a principle each one should restrict to that,&quot; he told reporters. &quot;We are doing our part so we expect others to do the same.&quot;</p>
<p>He said that the return of limited Iraqi oil exports would be &quot;no problem at all for the market.&quot;</p>
<p>At current prices Iraq would supply between 500-600,000 barrels per day to the market, Rakad said.</p>
</text>
